WEBVTT

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.000
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.800
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.430
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.100
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.100
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.430
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.430
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.290
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.460
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.010
Episode 23

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.010
Mayhem! The 6th Chaos Emerald

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.750
We've been waiting for you.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:52.130
Is that it?

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:57.510
Yes. After recovering and analyzing Eggman's robot, we created that prototype.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:02.640
Its code name is 'Beetle'. We're only one step away from completion.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:09.520
The President is waiting, so complete it as quickly as possible.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:11.860
You can count on me.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.580
They're beautiful.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.540
Jewels are the best.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:30.830
Thief!

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:33.170
I haven't stolen anything yet!

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.840
But that means you already have a plan.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:42.850
Everyone, be careful! There's a thief here!

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:49.690
You have such a great personality.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:52.980
I want you to call me the Beautiful Thief Rouge instead.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.820
It doesn't matter what I call you. A thief is a thief.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:20.930
Welcome.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:26.060
You must be Mr. Nelson Thorndyke. Are you looking for something?

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:29.890
I'm looking for a gift for my wife.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.240
What's this?

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:47.870
You're blessed with great intuition. This is our store's featured item.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:00.970
This is fantastic. This will be perfect for Lindsey.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:03.840
Hurry up and make this into a ring.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.390
A ring with a gem this large?

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:10.520
It has to be this big for Lindsey.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:14.270
Not only is she an actress, but this will also be our wedding anniversary present.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:22.820
I can picture Lindsey's smile. Oh, make it a size 8. Lindsey has very thin fingers.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:31.660
Thank you for your purchase. We hope to see you again.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:40.340
Hello. This is the Thorndyke residence.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.590
Hi, Tanaka. How are you?

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:48.350
Sir, it's been awhile.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:53.850
Yes, everyone is the same as ever.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:57.730
Why is Mr. Tanaka bowing at the wall?

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:05.570
He's not bowing at the wall. He's bowing to the person on the other end of the line. He's very polite.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:09.370
Chris, the master is on the line.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:10.950
Okay.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:13.750
The master? Is he talking about Chuck?

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.370
No.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:19.210
Thank you. Hello? Dad?

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:21.800
Yes, I'm fine. How about you?

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:27.800
The master is Chris's father. Chuck is Chris's father's father, so…

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:30.680
i refer to him as the great master.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.930
Do you understand now?

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:34.890
Yes I do.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:40.110
Oh, where's Mom? She's filming a movie at Filmdom City.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:46.610
She said that she won't be back until next week... Okay, I understand.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:52.240
Driver, take me to Filmdom City.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:53.450
Yes, sir.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:02.550
I don't know why, but my dad asked us all to go to Filmdom City.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:09.260
Filmdom City? Where they make all the movies? Hooray! I'm going!

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.890
Aren't we lucky, Amy?

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:19.810
Now we're set.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:23.610
Tails, how many more Emeralds do you need?

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:28.860
We have four and Knuckles has one. So two more.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.240
That means you only need a few more.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:37.540
But we still have to be careful when we encounter a new Emerald.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:43.090
The four Emeralds here have adapted to each other, so they're fine.

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:51.220
However, if we add a new Emerald, they will repel each other violently and unleash powerful electromagnetic waves.

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:55.970
It takes time for Emeralds to adapt to one another.

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:58.480
It must be difficult.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:03.110
Forget about these explanations. Let's hurry up and go!

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:04.570
Sorry.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:19.000
A city of movies. Sounds like fun.

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:33.890
X-Tornado!

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:40.310
Where are Sonic and the others going?

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.040
Come in.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:07.210
Dad!

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:08.300
Chris!

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:09.340
Dad!

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:12.220
I'm glad you came. I was waiting for you.

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:19.350
Sonic.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.890
Your recent race was amazing.

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:25.270
Oh thanks!

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:29.360
Dad, I want to introduce you to Sonic's friends.

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:31.190
This is Tails.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:32.610
Hi.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:33.990
Amy.

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:35.360
Hello.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:36.990
Cream and Cheese.

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:38.990
It's nice to meet you.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:41.290
And this is my teacher, Mr. Stewart.

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:44.500
Mr. Stewart? When did he arrive?

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:47.330
Nice to meet you. I'm Chris's homeroom teacher.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:50.250
How is Chris doing in school?

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:53.010
He is an excellent student.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:58.350
Forget about that. Nelson, why did you want us to come?

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:02.430
Oh that's right. The fact is…

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:05.730
Let's begin the final scene!

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:08.610
Ready, action!

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:17.070
Everyone left me behind. I'm all alone.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:24.080
You're…

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:29.880
Ferguson!

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:34.970
Darling?

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:39.850
I love you, Lindsey. This is for you.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:44.890
Do you remember what today is?

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:48.650
Congratulations on your wedding anniversary!

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:52.980
Chris! Everyone! My darling...

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:55.150
Congratulations!

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:00.160
Thank you, my darling.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:05.000
So that's the story!

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.120
In other words…

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:11.130
Just before they film the scene, Mr. Thorndyke and the actor exchange places.

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:14.840
You want to surprise your wife?

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:16.300
Exactly.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:20.550
A surprise wedding anniversary party sounds great!

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:25.140
That's a splendid idea.

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:30.400
Ella, what do you think of this ring?

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:39.240
How magnificent!

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.490
It's reacting.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:00.840
I'm bored.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:04.810
Totally.

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:09.770
This is... Dr. Eggman, it's the Chaos Emerald!

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.610
Chaos Emerald?

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:17.150
Really? Where?

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:19.820
Filmdom City!

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:24.160
Full speed ahead to Filmdom City!

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:41.220
The Chaos Emerald is reacting to something.

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:46.970
It led me to this location.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.520
What's that?

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:27.970
What happened?

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:32.350
Anyway, go change in the other room. There's not much time left.

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:34.390
You're right.

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:40.650
It's a real Chaos Emerald.

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:46.700
Sonic, that gem is a Chaos Emerald. What should we do?

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:52.160
Why was the Chaos Emerald turned into a ring for an anniversary gift?

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:57.330
Let's think about what to do after the surprise party is over.

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:06.640
This is Teacher. I discovered a gem that might be a Chaos Emerald. I'm going to retrieve it.

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:29.950
Hey, Sonic.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:32.620
Knuckles, how are you?

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:34.830
What's the commotion?

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:37.120
It's a long story.

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:42.460
Okay! Begin the final scene!

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:45.760
Ready, action!

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:53.350
Everyone left me behind. I'm all alone.

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:00.020
You're…

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:02.320
Lindsay...

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:10.450
Oops!

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:13.200
Darling?

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:14.410
Lindsay...

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:33.890
There's a strong signal!

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:35.430
There it is.

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.060
What?

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:44.150
It's the light from a Chaos Emerald! Charge!

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:55.330
Hurry up and put the Emerald away!

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:08.630
Are you all right, Mrs. Thorndyke? Mr. Thorndyke?

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:14.180
What's the meaning of this? Thanks to you, the entire studio is a mess!

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:16.470
I didn't think things were going to turn out this way.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:19.730
We made mother angry.

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:22.850
You don't have to say it like that!

00:15:22.850 --> 00:15:28.650
What! Don't you realize how hard I had to work to get a role in this movie?

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:30.990
I did this to make you happy!

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:35.280
Did this for me? This was horrible!

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:37.450
Both of you, calm down.

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:38.950
Shut up!

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:42.420
Mr. and Mrs. Thorndyke have begun arguing.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:44.920
Sonic, that reaction was...

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:47.750
Yeah. It's most likely a Chaos Emerald.

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:50.510
Then let's hurry up and retrieve it.

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:53.550
There's a bit of a problem...

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:54.970
What was that?

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:03.400
Chaos Emerald!

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:06.230
Eggman? Not him again.

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:13.280
I'm over here.

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:18.790
Stop, Sonic!

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:44.980
Things are getting complicated. Let's finish this job quickly.

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:46.350
Rouge!

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:48.940
The ring!

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:53.360
Thief! Give me back the ring!

00:16:53.610 --> 00:17:00.580
I can't give it back because this is no ordinary gem. It's a Chaos Emerald.

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:06.920
This is a Chaos Emerald? It indeed is a Chaos Emerald!

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:08.590
Give it back, Eggman!

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:10.710
No way, you fool!

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:11.920
Rouge!

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:13.970
Hand over the Emerald!

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:18.300
Decoe! Bocoe! I have the Chaos Emerald! Let's get out of here!

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:20.890
Whoa, okay!

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:22.520
Okay!

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:28.230
Eggman stole the Chaos Emerald.

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:34.030
Give it back, Eggman!

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:36.400
Be quiet!

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:47.210
Don't come this way!

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.210
Eggman!

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:53.420
Give us back the Chaos Emerald!

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:55.470
Idiots!

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:58.390
Come, E-74!

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:12.320
Eggman's robot!

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:26.790
Stop! Don't you dare come near my family!

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:28.670
Wait!

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:42.050
My job is to protect the Thorndyke family!

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:56.400
Even if I have to die to protect- Ahhh!

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:00.660
What's up with him?

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:03.830
He is a nice guy.

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:21.470
I'll face you!

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:27.640
Don't forget about me!

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:34.110
Come on!

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:42.240
We have the Chaos Emerald.

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:44.160
It's a Chaos Emerald ring.

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:45.780
It shines brilliantly.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.600
Oh no! It's a dead end!

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:15.980
Damn, this is bad!

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:21.440
Sonic! Sonic! Where are you?

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:28.280
Sonic is underwater?

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:38.550
It's an aquarium.

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:42.010
Damn!

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:45.430
Sonic! Jump up!

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:10.450
We'll let them off the hook for today.

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:11.330
Right.

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:12.120
Yeah.

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:16.210
Goodbye!

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:19.500
Lindsey! Chris!

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:21.090
Darling!

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:23.840
I'm glad that you're both safe.

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:26.800
What a crazy wedding anniversary.

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:32.720
The thief stole the ring. And it was such a gorgeous gem.

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:37.600
I must atone for my failure by slicing open my stomach!

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:42.780
Tanaka! Even without the ring, today is still the wedding anniversary.

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:46.700
That's right. Besides, you mean more to me than a ring.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:47.860
Ma'am...

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:52.160
Dad! Mom! Congratulations on your anniversary!

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:54.370
Congratulations!

00:21:56.710 --> 00:21:59.330
Thank you, everyone.

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:09.970
At least it was a happy ending.

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:14.140
Yeah, other than Eggman stealing the Chaos Emerald.

00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:18.440
Sonic has four and Knuckles has one.

00:22:18.810 --> 00:22:23.610
And Eggman has one Chaos Emerald.

00:22:24.610 --> 00:22:29.280
If all seven Chaos Emeralds are collected, they can create a miracle.

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:32.160
I will get them all.

00:22:35.870 --> 00:22:42.210
This is Teacher. I failed to acquire the Chaos Emerald.

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:54.450
<b>Watashitachi no sekai wa mahou o kakerarete</b>

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:54.450
<i>There’s magic cast on our world.</i>

00:22:54.450 --> 00:23:03.420
<b>Ai suru to kime kisae namida ni ujirareteru</b>

00:22:54.450 --> 00:23:03.420
<i>The nervousness of love is sealed by tears.</i>

00:23:03.420 --> 00:23:12.300
<b>Boy boy futari de jumon wo sagashi ni ikou</b>

00:23:03.420 --> 00:23:12.300
<i>Boy, let’s search for a spell together,</i>

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:21.900
<b>Kinji rareta yume wo kanaerareru kuni he</b>

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:21.900
<i>To a land where our forbidden dreams can come true.</i>

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:30.840
<b>Dare ni mo naisho de ashita na tchi awaseshiyou</b>

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:30.840
<i>Let’s secretly meet tomorrow.</i>

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:41.040
<b>Itsuka kotori wo ume ta yowake no mieru oka de</b>

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:41.040
<i>At the place where we buried the bird, the hill where we can see the sunrise.</i>

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:49.800
<b>Tsumetai asamoya kimi to te wo tsunaidara</b>

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:49.800
<i>In the cold morning mist, if I hold hands with you.</i>

